     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "On the beach Ravi felt a cool wind blowing from the sea in the afternoon.\n\"That is the sea breeze,\" said his uncle."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "sea breeze",
     "land breeze",
     "convection"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "In the day the land heats faster than the sea. Warm air over land rises and cool air from the sea moves in. This is a sea breeze.\nAt night the land cools faster, so the wind blows from land to sea. This is a land breeze.\nWe wear light-coloured cotton in summer because it reflects heat, and dark wool in winter because it absorbs and keeps heat in."
    }
